// COLCON - conditions on b for AX=b to be consistent (column space constraints).
// Row-reduce [A|I]; rows of the right block next to zero rows of A give c with c.b = 0.
// Out: [C] = constraint rows (AX=b consistent  <=>  [C]*b = 0)
ClrHome
Disp "CONSTRAINTS ON B","FOR AX=B CONSISTENT"
dim([A])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→G
ʟZD(2)→U
augment([A],identity(G))→[J]
0→S
0→Q
U→W
prgmZRREF
If R=G:Then
Disp "RANK = NUMBER OF ROWS","ALWAYS CONSISTENT","(COLS SPAN R^M)"
Return
End
{G-R,G}→dim([C])
For(I,1,G-R)
For(J,1,G)
[J](R+I,U+J)→[C](I,J)
End
End
[C]→[J]
0→W
prgmZRREF
[J]→[C]
Disp "CONSISTENT IFF","[C]*B = 0, I.E. EACH ROW","C OF [C] HAS C.B = 0"
Pause [C]►Frac
